speechtext:
There have been discussions among the Parties and I appreciate the co-operation of the Opposition Members in coming to the following agreement which I think will meet the acceptance of the Members of the House. Before reading the motion, I should say that there is an understanding among the Parties that the items on the projected Order of Business for today, namely Bill C-148 and Bill C-153 will be dealt with in all stages by one o'clock p.m. today.
August 25, 1988

The motion I have to put to the House is this. I move:
That the House shall complete its consideration of Bill C-139, an Act to amend the Income Tax Act, the Canada Pension Plan, the Unemployment Insurance Act, 1971, the Federal-Provincial Fiscal Arrangements and Federal Post-Secondary Education and Health Contributions Act, 1977 and certain related Acts, by Friday, August 26, 1988, but with any division or divisions deferred until six o'clock p.m. Monday, August 29, 1988;
That Monday, August 29, 1988 and Tuesday, August 30, 1988, shall be designated as the two days allotted for third reading stage of Bill C-130, an Act to implement the Free Trade Agreement between Canada and the United States of America, pursuant to the order made August 16, 1988;
That any division requested on Bill C-130 shall be deferred until three o'clock p.m. on Wednesday, August 31, 1988;
That, following any such deferred division, or as the first order of Government business on Wednesday, August 31, 1988, as the case may be, Bill C-114, an Act to provide for greater certainty in the reconciliation of the personal interests and duties of office of Members of the Senate and of the House of Commons, to establish a Conflict of Interest Commission and to make consequential amendments to other Acts, shall be called for second reading;
That second reading of Bill C-114 and voting on any question related thereto shall be completed not later than 5.45 o'clock p.m., Thursday, September 1, 1988.
That on that day, immediately following such proceedings, the House shall stand adjourned until 11 o'clock a.m. Tuesday, September 13, 1988, provided that (a) the provision of Standing Orders 5 and 68(3) and 68(4) shall remain in effect during such adjournment; (b) if necessary, at the request of the Government during such adjournment, Mr. Speaker shall fix a time for the purpose of the giving of Royal Assent to any Bills which have not been given Royal Assent, and that after the giving of Royal Assent to any such Bills, the House shall stand adjourned to the time and the day stated in this order; and
That, the reports of the legislative committees on Bill C-144, an Act to authorize payments by Canada toward the provision of child care services, and to amend the Canada Assistance Plan in consequence thereof, and Bill C-136, an Act respecting broadcasting and to amend certain Acts in relation thereto and in relation to radio communication, (if they have not been tabled) shall be receivable by the Clerk of the House during such adjournment and shall be deemed to have been reported and stand on the Order Paper for report stage consideration on or after Tuesday, September 13, 1988, provided, that, the Notice Paper shall remain open until six o'clock p.m. on Monday, September 12, 1988, for the sole purpose of receiving report stage motions to either of these Bills.
